<section class="blk blk--first">
  <p class="eyebrow">The Movement</p>
  <h1 class="sec">The Movement.</h1>
  <p class="lead">From agreement to action — one front door.</p>
  <p>Most people already know living costs too much. The Movement turns that into something organised: reach people with something true and worth sharing, welcome them in, and give them a clear way to act. Everything we publish leads back to the evidence — and to a way to take part.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">How it reaches people</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Short, visual, source-led — never outrage alone.</h2>
  <p>Explainers and data pieces, in the movement’s own illustrated style, shared where attention already is — and carried further by people who share them with their own audiences. The rule doesn’t bend: every public piece leads back to a source and a way to help, never outrage on its own.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">Ways in</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Three ways in.</h2>
  <div class="scope">
    <div>
      <h3>The Pledge</h3>
      <p>A short public statement of what the movement stands for. Signing is free and opens at launch; sharing it onward is how the count grows. <a href="/pledge">Read the pledge →</a></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>The cost-of-living quiz <span class="status status--planned">Planned</span></h3>
      <p>Guess what living actually costs — a short test that teaches something surprising, with the full breakdown when you join.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Share-a-stat <span class="status status--planned">Planned</span></h3>
      <p>Ready-made, sourced cost-of-living facts as graphics and short clips, for supporters to repost to their own networks. Only published, source-backed figures ever become share assets.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--ink">
